.TH WMMAIL 1
.SH NAME
wm/mail \- Tk mail client over the upas file system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/mail
[
.B -f
.I mbox
] [
.B -m
.I mailbox
]
.br
.B wm/mail
.B -i
.B -u
.I user
.B -P
.I passfile
[
.B -s
.I server
] [
.B -a
.I dialip
] [
.B -p
.I port
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Wm/mail
is a graphical mail reader.
It drives
.IR upas/fs (1)'s
.B /mail/fs
namespace and presents the mailbox as a scrolling list of messages with a
header pane and a body pane; it deletes through
.B /mail/fs/ctl
and (in the interactive window) replies through
.IR upas-send (1).
Unlike the older
.IR readmail (1)
it speaks no plaintext POP3 \(em all transport is the
.IR tls12 (2)-based
upas backend, so it works with modern servers.
.PP
With
.B -f
it serves a local Unix mbox; with
.B -i
it fetches an IMAP mailbox over TLS (see
.IR upas-fetch (1)
for the
.BR -s / -a / -p / -u / -P
options).
If
.B /mail/fs
is already served,
.I wm/mail
uses it and neither option is needed.
.B -m
selects the mailbox name (default
.BR mbox ).
.PP
Selecting a message in the list shows it; the
.BR Prev ,
.BR Next ,
.B Delete
and
.B Sync
buttons navigate, remove and re-read.
.SS Self-test
.B -t
runs a headless self-test used by
.IR tests (see SOURCE): it starts the backend, reads the mailbox, prints the
message list and the first message, and exits without opening a window.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/mail.b
.br
.B /tests/wmmail.sh
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR upas/fs (1),
.IR upas-fetch (1),
.IR upas-send (1),
.IR nedmail (1),
.IR readmail (1)
.SH BUGS
Composing a new message and interactive reply are minimal; the reader half is
the focus.
